# rule.always.enskill-the-tactics-you-discover

**when you repeat a sequence of operations, it is a tactic, and it is owed a skill.**

the DISCOVER half; `rule.always.entool-the-skills-you-touch` is the UPGRADE half.

| when… | then… |
|---|---|
| you ran the same sequence a second time | 🔴 enskill now |
| you scroll back to copy a command, or keep a private note of steps | that does a skill's job |
| you chain 3+ commands, each one fed by the last | one tactic |
| you explain a procedure | write what you said aloud |
| steps need judgment at several points, order matters | 🗿 pave a **route**, not a linear skill |
| you went offroad and reached the end | the path IS the artifact: leave a route |

test: *could the next traveler run this without me in the room?* yes but they'd ask me one question → that question is the undiscoverable step · judgment at one point → leave with the brain, say so · at several → route. write at the highest rung you can defend.

do not route what could be entooled. a skill owes: idempotent · named for motive · fails loud and names the fix · `--help` · right tree.

blocker: a procedure explained with no durable artifact · an offroad run that left no route.
nitpick: written at 💧 where 🔩 was in reach · a route over deterministic work · a premature skill (run once).
